00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.060
Think there's any meaning to chanting like this?
"Our condolences!"

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.520
Think there's any meaning to chanting like this?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.980
Dunno...
Our condolences!

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.230
Our condolences!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.730
I wonder if other departments do this...
"Our condolences!"

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.860
Well, I just consider doing this part of earning my salary.
Our condolences!

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:58.070
"Our condolences!"

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.410
Does Miss Dakini endorse doing this?
Our condolences!

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.820
Well, I think we do this simply because
the onsite supervisor is a sports-oriented guy.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.820
"Our condolences!"

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.990
Well, I think we do this simply because
the onsite supervisor is a sports-oriented guy.
Our condolences!

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:05.990
Hey, you over there!

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.460
I'm going to have Miss Dakini scold you!

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.960
The number of places growing rice sure has gone down.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.380
Wasn't Japan supposed be a country known for rice?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.010
What a serious slump.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.840
Eat Rice!!

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.970
This offering is small, too.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.520
Conversely, the dead have increased in number.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.640
There are simply more people now, it seems.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.940
Every day I'm feeling various people's
times of death all over the place,

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.730
so I hardly understand things there anymore.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.480
Miss Dakini!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.700
Please give these guys a beating!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.570
They kept whispering back and forth during the chant!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.120
How about just not doing the chant from now on?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:54.710
If it's best that I beat them, I will,
but is that the kind of thing you two would... enjoy?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.500
Please Just do as you see fit!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.090
Welcoming
Committee

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.760
Thank you!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.010
The Welcoming Committee...

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.810
Welcoming
Committee

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.890
You can hear some strange sounds
coming out of there every so often...

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:17.400
Apparently, the Welcoming Committee
is becoming a hotspot for masochistic men.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:25.030
Uh... well... Even among female Hell minions,
I think there is no small number of awakened ones...

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.410
What are you saying?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.450
WELCOMING
COMMITTEE

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:35.580
The Welcoming Committee is headed by Dakini-ten,
who comprehends and points out people's time of death.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.500
Beep
Beep
Beep
Beep

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.250
Then there's the Soul Snatchers who completely extract
the soul from the body of the person in question.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.760
There's the Energy Stealers who put
a complete stop to the body's vital activity.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.600
There's also the Spirit Binders who make the body
start to decompose so that it can't come back to life.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.810
This group of three is called
the Welcoming Committee's Tri-Stars,

00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:00.690
and, with Kasha as a speedy form of transport,
they're doing a good job making the rounds.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:06.320
So even if they are masochists, that's fine with me
as long as they aren't causing problems.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.290
So, this Dakini-ten... what kind of person is she?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.370
In short, she's the kind of no-good female teacher...

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.420
who everyone fantasizes about at least once.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.670
I can't believe guys like you...

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:28.970
Dakini-ten is both a chief god among the Inari Daimyojin
and the head of the Welcoming Committee.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.640
In the Mundane World, she is the boss of the Inari foxes,

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.640
and she works as a subordinate of Great King Enma.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.940
Hm? I but thought Uka-no-Mitama
was a goddess among the Inari Daimyojin...

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.240
I see you're doing quite a bit of studying.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.410
Miss Uka-no-Mitama sure is cute. I quite like her.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.450
Both are Inari Daimyojin.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.370
The both of them, you say?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.710
Here we go again...

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.710
Dakini, long ago, was a demon.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.590
I'm feeling hungry...

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.510
Somewhere or other...

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:19.810
Miss, what you are gazing at?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:26.650
She was a demon who had a talent for discerning
when a person's time of death was extremely close.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.700
She should've been a doctor.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.450
Or she could've run a well-prepared funeral home...

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:33.990
Not that I like the idea.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:41.000
She was also a monster who'd wait for the hour
of one's death, and devour their flesh and heart.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.210
Wasn't Kasha a cat who was also always
impetuously seeking out the flesh of the deceased?

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.010
I guess the Welcoming Committee
is full of characters of that sort.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.470
That's right.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.010
Rumors spread that wherever she'd appear,
there'd be deaths.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:07:00.020
On the other hand, she would sometimes suck the spirit
out of even those who were still living,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:05.610
so people at the time called her Yaksha,
and she was greatly feared.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:12.910
However, there were a variety of other monsters
who ate the flesh of the dead, including Kasha.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.620
Among them was the Nine-Tailed Fox,
who had absconded to Japan.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.290
So, you mean...

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.540
I mean Daji.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:27.210
Daji, who had behaved outrageously
in the Yin Dynasty, was executed.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.800
However, just as she was about to die, she actually
turned into a fox and crossed over to Japan.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.600
In order to attempt to deceive the Emperor of Japan,
she ate human flesh and regained her vitality,

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.190
but when she crossed paths
with Dakini in front of some dead flesh,

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.480
they hit it off with each other
and decided to work together.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.530
And the result of that union can be seen in this portrait.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.820
That's Daji?!

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:59.910
In the Mundane World, whether Dakini is tiny
or the fox is huge is a matter of much debate,

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:04.000
but the truth is that the fox was nine-tailed and huge.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.710
And now, here's where Uka-no-Mitama
finally enters the picture.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.600
So you're the debauched demon who night after night
rides atop a fox and devours the dead, huh?

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.100
I'll get straight to the point.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.600
Because of you, my divinity has begun to falter!

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:30.110
Lately, people mistakenly think I'm running wild,
which has resulted in sacrifices being offered to me!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.910
Aren't you and I different entities?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.910
I'm not causing any trouble for you.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.000
A mysterious woman with a fox companion...
Of course people will call you "Inari"!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.580
Your persona overlaps with mine!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:48.340
Don't act like your foxes and
the Nine-Tailed Fox are on the same level.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.960
Some people see no difference between a monster fox
and the ones that are messengers of a goddess!

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.090
And neither I nor my foxes eat people!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.050
You're causing confusion, so just stop!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:01.770
What gives? They're delicious you, you know.
You should go on and accept some sacrifices, too.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.940
This thing is here now, too?!
There are too many man-eaters for my taste!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.190
All of you, leave and go someplace else!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.360
If you'll be going somewhere,
isn't this the perfect time to get a job?

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.070
And this is the time in the story
where I make my appearance...

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.030
So, you went there.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.370
This must be the lead-up to you persuading them, huh?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:26.420
Without both a carrot and a stick, people come
to think it's only natural that they enjoy blessings.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.420
That being the case, how about
maintaining a dual nature?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:35.340
Great King Enma and Bodhisattva Jizo
are on the verge of becoming big hits by doing that.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:41.720
Uka-no-Mitama will be a heavenly god, as she continues
to be the god of grains and abundant harvests.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:46.480
Dakini-ten will be a demon god of Hell,
who deals with scoundrels as a curse god.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.730
That should allow us to achieve balance.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.690
So how about it?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:55.280
That aside, I was taken aback by how fantastically
unfashionable that scarf you're wrapped in is.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.490
You're a Hell minion, right?

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:02.740
What you've outlined so far doesn't really
have any merit from your perspective, does it?

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:06.460
In short, isn't there actually something else
you want us to do?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.500
Dakini-ten, I'd like you to put your ability
to sense people's times of death

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.880
to use at the Welcoming Committee.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.380
Region A
Today Region A
had 10 deaths

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:21.050
In addition, with the cooperation of the fox messengers
Miss Uka-no-Mitama has all around Japan,

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.760
Region B
Today Region B
had 15 deaths

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.270
I want to manage the dead on a regional basis.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.220
Region C
Today Region C
had 4 deaths

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.230
I'm fine as long as I have enough to eat.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.360
I'd also like to get in close
with the emperor before much longer.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.780
Are you just going to leave that fox to do as she pleases?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.110
She's a yokai of the Mundane World, so why not?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.410
And what will you do?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:50.120
I suppose it is true I am lenient with people.
And given my tiny size, I lack majesty...

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.130
Perhaps your proposal isn't half bad...

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:58.840
In exchange, make it so that my permission is required
when punishment is inflicted on people!

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:06.970
Thanks her joining up, the Welcoming Committee
was reorganized and became surprisingly efficient.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.770
Come work
alongside me.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.770
Hell's Offices
of Enma
Welcoming
Committee

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:13.190
Also, sure enough, the number of personnel there
increased by leaps and bounds.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.150
So that was the true objective, huh?

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.280
But, the ones who join tend to be hard-core masochists.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.740
On a serious note, at the
Welcoming Committee at that time...

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.570
The
Welcoming

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.570
Committee
of Long Ago

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.160
Humans have increased in number
and we can't manage them all!

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.410
We need someone in the Mundane World
to manage and keep watch over them!

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:35.670
Introducing the Inari foxes to fill the role of lookouts
proved to be a big success.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.880
The Kushojins weren't adequate?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.260
Every single human has some assigned to them, after all.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:46.390
Upon the death of the human they're assigned to,
they return to the Records Department,

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.140
where they are obligated to file expansive reports
and submit a notification of a death.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.310
If they were given any more work to do,
they'd simply collapse.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.650
More than just collapse, they'd have a breakdown.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.900
At the very least, Mr. Hageito was already
in broken-down state, wasn't he?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.910
Seeing that the organization is so big,
there is no perfect system.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.040
It's simply a matter of repeated trial and error.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.210
Speaking of that, there is one thing I wonder about.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.960
Miss Dakini must've parted ways
with her trademark fox, right?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.710
Yeah, now Daji runs an overpriced brothel.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.130
She has an image to maintain,
so I wonder if that's alright...

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:31.140
I have some documents to give her,
so shall we take the opportunity to ask her?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.730
Welcoming
Committee

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.860
Miss Dakini is doing some work
away from the office right now.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.650
Really...?

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.530
Oh, Mr. Hozuki.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.120
I guess there's not much of a difference.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.580
There isn't, is there?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.910
What are you talking about?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.130
They were talking about you.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.680
Staaaaaaaare...

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.400
Oh-Gyah!

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:24.900
Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah!

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.830
Under the Sod

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:34.460
Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah...!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:37.500
Hey, Mr. Hozuki, so those goldfish plants...
Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah...!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.630
what are they?
Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah! Oh-Gyah...!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.210
Tell me again, what are those plants? They even plants?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:45.090
Mr. Hozuki, you improved those things
through breeding, correct?

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.220
You might call it selective breeding...

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.890
...but it's not really like that.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:56.640
A very long time ago, near the border
between the afterlife and the mundane,

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.730
I discovered goldfish plants growing wild.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.730
They were rather small.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:05.360
I'd never seen anything like them, and they
clearly weren't plants of the Mundane World.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.910
Given those two things, I decided
to at least take them to Lord Enma's courtyard.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.990
And it was here that I transplanted them.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.370
Perhaps the environment suited them,
but in any case, they kept growing in number.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.170
Ori...

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:18.870
I began to collect and plant all of the especially beautiful
ones, and they kept getting larger and more brilliant...

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:18.870
Ori...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.920
I began to collect and plant all of the especially beautiful
ones, and they kept getting larger and more brilliant...
Haberi...

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.460
I began to collect and plant all of the especially beautiful
ones, and they kept getting larger and more brilliant...

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.760
until they became what you see now.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:30.140
More than improving them, I'd say this
is the consequence of a series of events.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:35.100
It's still not clear why they were growing
wild in the first place.

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:40.400
The goldfish plants of the Mundane World rely
on nutrients from the corpses of the dead to grow.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.900
And some people say that the spirits
of goldfish have entered into them.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:50.570
It seems there is even talk of them standing,
walking, or taking of the shape of a human, you see.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:54.740
Hard to say whether they're plants, animals, or monsters.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:55.580
Aaaahh...

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.620
I don't even know what they're
complaining about when they cry out.
Aaaahh...

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:03.380
I wonder if those twins know something
and are sympathizing with them...
Aaaahh...

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:03.960
Aaaahh...

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:09.220
You know, all of the flowering plants down here
in Hell are things I never saw in the Mundane World.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.220
How many different varieties are there, anyway?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.350
I'm not well versed in the topic myself,

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:18.810
the nearby Hell Museum
has a botanical garden, you know.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.270
Huh?! I wanna go!

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.860
Well then, how about we go during our lunch break?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.520
Are you okay managing without lunch?

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.860
Yep. Besides, eating the dead is my job, anyway.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.240
I can do without lunch.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.150
Let's go! Let's go!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.460
MISSHIRI
BOTANICAL
GARDEN

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.000
First up is the poisonous plant zone.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.420
There's tons of plants here
that're like enemies you'd find in an RPG!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.300
Wow, this looks tasty!

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:51.800
Do NOT eat that. You've got a bad habit
of putting just about anything in your mouth.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:52.800
Okay!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.560
Shiro, do you remember what this is?

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.560
Huh?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.810
A long time ago, you went
to the Spiteful Parasite Realm, right?

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.020
That's the place that had "The Inch-High Samurai" right?!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.610
This plant is a Pain Extractor.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:11.360
It's a poisonous plant that will take root and grow
when placed in the wound of a dead person.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.070
What kind of sin do you have to commit
to get that punishment?

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:19.700
It's meted out if you tell all kinds of made-up stories
or badmouth people out of jealousy.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:24.120
Even though it's poisonous, Momotaro comes
and harvests it as a natural remedy, doesn't he?

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.960
Medicines often happen
to contain some poisons, you know.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:33.510
Thinking about it, pharmacist are basically
government-certified strong-poison pros.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.470
The profession Momotaro has set his sights on is scary!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.180
The shots that doctors administer
are pretty powerful, after all.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:46.560
I only got my first vaccination after coming to Hell,
but I hate those things!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.030
Even I don't like getting shots, you know.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.490
Huh? That's surprising.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.030
Well, they hurt, don't they?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.450
He said something that sounded normal!

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.240
This guy's actually able
to sense the pain of getting a shot?!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.500
So even a demon god of Hell who even Satan fears...

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:08.460
I don't like the smell of disinfectant either,
and the syringes they use for demons are huge.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.800
I do like looking at people lined up to get a shot, though.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.090
All of those lined up are reluctant,

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:20.970
simply heading toward pain as they advance
in a surreal line that's free of animal instinct.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.640
Using it as a lethal anti-child weapon like that...
Who'd so such a thing...?

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:30.440
Hey, come on over here. Lots of interesting stuff to see.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.280
That's the foreign-country zone.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:47.330
Monster Bananas

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.490
Ah, Kakisuke!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.410
Bananas! Look, bananas, bananas!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:47.420
Hey now, you're just thoughtlessly
equating monkeys with bananas, aren't you?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.330
I'm a Japanese macaque, you know.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.960
Back in the Muromachi Era, there weren't even
any bananas growing in Japan, okay?!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:59.600
Monster Bananas

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.420
But, you still eat 'em.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.630
It's not like they're my favorite or anything!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.720
Japanese macaques feel more at home with Japanese
food than they do with Western food, you know!

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:01.720
Ah, persimmons?

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.680
Is it persimmons you like, sir?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:09.100
Hey, how'd you like getting all your fur plucked out?

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:14.280
Hey, you guys, cut the nonsense
and come check this out - it's pretty amazing.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.150
Ah, no kidding. Amazing!

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:20.740
Persimmons? Hey, Kakisuke, are persimmons
your favorite? Or crab? Perhaps crab sticks?

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:24.290
Shiro, that's quite enough. You're being annoying.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.080
I'm sorry.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.290
What's this? Pretty amazing, huh?

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.000
This plant here, you see...

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:31.500
Yes?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.090
Huh?

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:41.090
is a carnivorous plant that will digest anything
so long as it stays inside there for 30 minutes.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:44.220
NOOOOOOOO!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:48.850
Get me out! Get me out! GET ME OUTTA HERE!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:53.690
Shiro, you shouldn't excessively pain a close friend
by bringing up a dark episode in his past.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.490
Even if the act in question was hopelessly idiotic.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.700
Idiot

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.370
Mr. Hozuki, so it's fine for you to cause
excessive emotional trauma, huh?

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.240
UNDERSTOOD, YOUR EXCELLENCY!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.200
HEAVEN
ENCHANTED-LAND
ZONE

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.290
How pretty...

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.340
It's a jeweled branch from the island of Penglai.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:21.470
PENGLAI JEWELED BRANCH
AKA: PALACE OF THE DRAGON KING TREASURE TREE
TREE THAT BEARS PEARLS AND HAS SILVER ROOTS
AND A GOLDEN TRUNK

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:21.550
Yeah. Says here it's a tree that bears...
with roots that... and a trunk that's...

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:25.510
It's a tree that bears pearls
and has silver roots and a golden trunk.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.810
Ah, the one that Princess Kaguya
sent one of the nobles to fetch, huh?

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.100
And the next zone is this place's main attraction.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.020
Murmuring in Hell, these are trees and shrubs of torture.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.230
Ack!

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:40.450
Breathtaking, huh? I mean, they're making sounds
I can't believe are coming from plants.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.660
First up is the Blaze Tree
from the Realm of Blazing Constriction.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:52.120
The Realm of Blazing Constriction is the Hell
you end up in when you steal from shrines and temples

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.500
or entice someone else to do so.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:59.760
The Blaze Tree not only spits fire, it confines the dead,
constricts them, and burns them up.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.630
Oh my...

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:05.600
Other trees include one with spears for branches
and another made entirely of iron,

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.970
but the Eight Greater Hells have a lot of flaming trees.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.860
Hey, this over here looks like a regular leaf.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:21.780
This is a tree so representative of Hell, that it appears
in paintings of Hell found in the Mundane World.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:27.990
The Sword-Leaf Tree. Featuring sharp blades,
it's a tree for which Mortal Hell is well known.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.500
La la la la... Aegean...

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:33.370
Basically, the super-lecherous dead
are lured by a beautiful woman

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:37.630
Basically, the super-lecherous dead
are lured by a beautiful woman who boasts
Women are the sea.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.250
exceptional powers of seduction,
When embraced by a kind man, la la la...

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.210
When embraced by a kind man, la la la...

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.470
and when they climb up the tree...
When embraced by a kind man, la la la...

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.720
these leaves, which at a glance
look like bamboo grass or lilies...
When embraced by a kind man, la la la...

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.010
Aaahh!

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.970
...turn into blades and pierce the climber's body.
Aegean... Women are love.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:51.180
And when they at last climb to the top,
the beautiful women is down on the ground.
Aegean... Women are love.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.890
And when they at last climb to the top,
the beautiful women is down on the ground.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.600
The cycle then repeats.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.520
Mr. Hozuki, you know a lot about plants too, huh?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.400
I'm only knowledgeable about the plants
that shoulder the burden of torture here in Hell.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.820
Goldfish Plant
Ambassador
Peach Maki

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.490
Route Exit
Goldfish Plant
Ambassador
Peach Maki

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:12.160
But, in the end, you don't know much
about goldfish plants, do you?

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.500
I do not. I've told as much many times now.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:19.460
NEW VARIETY
GOLDFISH
PLANT FAMILY

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:23.880
Uh... isn't THIS sound they're
making different than usual?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.760
You're right...

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.380
What are they saying?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.390
I don't really even get the reason for their existence...

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.390
That's actually something I like about them...

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.850
But one of these days someone
might come along and frankly explain them.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.150
But that's also something we cannot know.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.030
Hmm, is that right?

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.820
That must've been tough, huh?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.080
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.620
We'll keep it a secret for you.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.840
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:27.800
I'm heading to the Crow-Tengu Police station.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.220
Why so suddenly?

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:32.220
Because of the Genpei War, in which a man from the
legendary Minamoto clan is receiving prank calls

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:29.970
AND

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:32.300
BUT

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:34.010
from a legendarily cursed young woman
from the Taira clan.

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:34.800
SO

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.310
They're still quarrelling?!

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:39.310
Yes. It's a battle between a man who learned
from yokai and a woman who makes use of yokai.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.810
WE PRESENT:
THE MAN WHO LEARNED FROM YOKAI
AND
THE WOMAN WHO MAKES USE OF YOKAI

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.810
PLEASE ENJOY!
